    "note": "candidate-002 — tightened candidate-001 per your notes (\"t=0 looks awkward, half dots seen; final state clips the final dot; animation is very premium\"). Both edge issues had one root cause: the first/last data points sat exactly ON the plot edges, so their marker halos overflowed (poked past the curtain's left edge at t=0; clipped against the card at the final frame). Fix: inset the data x-range by the halo radius so end markers sit fully inside, and pad the curtain UP into the headroom (covers a peak marker at the very top) while padding DOWN only a hair (so it never clips the month-label band). Now t=0 is a clean blank card with axes + labels, the wipe reveals everything, and the final state shows both end dots in full. (Captured your introLength→0.95 nudge as candidate-001_humanedits.mosaic; this candidate uses the template default 0.7 = ~1.4s wipe + ~0.6s hold on the final chart. Bump the Intro length slider if you want the longer wipe as the default.)",
